From d53bb10833198bac64a49e557749f604d0a45c6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:02:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] tcp: refresh BBR congestion control

Backport the current BBRv1 implementation from the S24 6.1 kernel,
bringing in the fixes and improvements accumulated since the 4.14
version:

- ack aggregation support (extra_acked), which avoids underestimating
  the delivery rate when ACKs are delayed or aggregated;
- better cwnd computation based on the BDP, a quantization budget and
  the packets in flight at the estimated delivery time, reducing
  bursts and bufferbloat;
- TSO segment sizing through tso_segs_goal() using the pacing rate
  and the MSS, capped at 0x7f segments;
- PROBE_RTT and min-RTT filter updates without the delayed-ACK
  special case.

The implementation is adapted to the 4.14 API: local tcp_snd_cwnd()
accessors, tcp_clock_ns() instead of tp->tcp_clock_cache,
tcp_tso_autosize() instead of sk_pacing_shift/GSO_LEGACY_MAX_SIZE,
and no BTF kfunc registration. struct bbr grows to 104 bytes, so
icsk_ca_priv is enlarged from 88 to 104 bytes (13 * sizeof(u64)),
matching the upstream change.

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: @Devandroid-bit.
