From 0fbd3af984f53107a603718b6fb06f7c9e7b5fe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:18:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] input: booster: refresh input booster to v2

Backport the current input booster implementation from the S24 6.1
sources, replacing the legacy evdev hooks with a dedicated input
handler and updating the event detection logic:

- capture input events through an input handler registered from
  evdev_booster late_initcall, instead of instrumenting evdev;
- aggregate events and trigger the booster from a dedicated
  workqueue, with the updated per-device key/type detection;
- rework the DT parser: resources are selected through
  allowed_resources, release values through ib_release_values and
  CPU cluster policies through cpu_cluster_policy;
- keep the Exynos 4.14 backend (UCC, KPP/stune and PM QoS) with
  the new long *qos_values / rel_flags interface.

The Exynos9820 DT does not provide allowed_resources,
cpu_cluster_policy or max_cluster_count, so those fall back to
the identity mapping (0..max_resource_count-1) and three CPU
clusters. CONFIG_SEC_INPUT_BOOSTER_SLSI and
CONFIG_SEC_INPUT_BOOSTER_HANDLER are enabled in the defconfig.

Signed-off-by: Devandroid-bit <180217512+Devandroid-bit@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: @Devandroid-bit.
